Graduate Civil Engineer
Civcon Civil & Project Management (Civcon) is a Western Australia Civil Construction and Project Management company, providing services to our niche client base. At Civcon, we pride ourselves on our outstanding service and ability to deliver complex civil construction and utilities projects to the highest standards of safety and quality.
We are currently seeking a graduate Civil Engineer to be part of the team, starting with our Tendering team at our West Perth Office. 
This is an entry-level opportunity to start your career as a Civil Engineer.
About the Role
- Completing quantity take-offs for tender submissions;
- Assisting in the preparation of calculations of materials, labour and equipment
- Preparation and issue of RFI’s;
- Preparation of and issue of RFQ’s;
- Reporting to the Senior Estimator or Estimating Manager on comparison of quotations; and
As you develop and learn on the job, you will be working towards working as a Site Engineer.
About You
- Bachelor of Engineering;
- Strong written and verbal communication skills with the ability to build rapport and to listen actively;
- High attention to detail and strong organisational
- Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, Outlook)
- A genuine passion for Engineering
- Demonstrated ability to meet deadlines, work within timeframes and deliver agreed targets.
- A proactive approach and willingness to learn from experienced team of Estimators and operational teams.
What this Position will provide you with
- Structured Civil Engineering development providing exposure to the civil construction industry;
- Perth metropolitan based projects;
- A competitive remuneration;
- An inclusive workplace;
- Full-time permanent position (not contract term);
- The opportunity to move into a Site Engineering position
Civcon is an equal opportunity employer and welcome applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders people and women.
